{key: Bb}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bbmaj7] | [Bbmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Noticing how the [Bb]guests chose the places of hon[Gm7]or
He told them a pa[Eb]rable to guide their [Bb]hearts
When you are in[Gm7]vited to a wedding feast
Do not take the [Dm7]place of honor for safety
For [Cm7]someone more distinguished may have been invit[F]ed
And [Eb]the host will ask you [F]to give this man your [Bb]place
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Go and take the [Eb]lowest place in[F]stead
So the host can say [Bb]friend move up to [F/A]a bet[Gm7]ter place
You will be hon[Eb]ored in front of all the [F]guests
